What is the name of the GI Bill passed after 9/11, and what is its significance?
The GI Bill passed after 9/11 is the Post-9/11 GI Bill, also known as the Post-9/11 Veterans Educational Assistance Act of 2008. Its significance is that it provides education benefits to military personnel who have served at least 90 days of active duty since September 10, 2001, and their families.
