What is the historical context of the Iwo Jima battle?
The historical context of the Iwo Jima battle is that it was a major battle in which the United States Marine Corps landed on and eventually captured the island of Iwo Jima from the Imperial Japanese Army (IJA) during World War II, specifically from February 19 to March 26, 1945. The American invasion, designated Operation Detachment, aimed to capture the entire island, including its three Japanese-controlled airfields, to provide a staging area for attacks on the Japanese main islands.
