What is the sequence and numbering of the months in the Jewish calendar?
Based on the provided context, the sequence and numbering of the months in the Jewish calendar are as follows:

1. Nisan (first month)
2. Iyyar (second month)
3. Sivan (third month)
4. Tammuz (fourth month)
5. Av (fifth month)
6. Elul (sixth month)
7. Tishrei (seventh month, but the first month of the new calendar year)
8. Marcheshvan (eighth month)
9. Kislev (ninth month)
10. Tevet (tenth month)
11. Shevat (eleventh month)
12. Adar (twelfth month)

Note that the numbering of the months may be adjusted to postpone Rosh Hashanah, but the above sequence is the standard order.
