Identify the context and purpose of the Atlanta Exposition
The context of the Atlanta Exposition refers to the Cotton States and International Exposition, which was held in Atlanta, Georgia in 1895. The purpose of the exposition was to:

* Promote the region to the world
* Showcase products and new technologies
* Encourage trade with Latin America
* Demonstrate the progress made since the city's destruction during the Battle of Atlanta and new developments in cotton production
* Announce an end to the Reconstruction Era and the sectional hostilities that had plagued the nation for several decades.

Additionally, the exposition also served as a platform for Booker T. Washington to deliver his famous "Atlanta Exposition Speech", which laid the foundation for the Atlanta compromise, an agreement between African-American leaders and Southern white leaders.
