What is the history of Peru's participation in the FIFA World Cup?
Peru first participated in the FIFA World Cup in 1930, where they lost both games and finished 10th out of 13 teams. They then withdrew or did not enter the next four tournaments (1934, 1938, 1950, and 1954). Peru participated but did not qualify in 1958, 1962, or 1966. Their best result was in Mexico 1970, where they finished in seventh place, advancing to the quarterfinals by defeating Bulgaria and Morocco, and losing to Germany and Brazil.
