What is the structure of a carrot, specifically the location of the seed within it?
The structure of a carrot is a taproot, meaning it grows underground and has a single main root. The seed of a carrot is located at the top of the root, near the soil surface. The seeds are typically found in a small cluster at the crown of the carrot, which is the part of the root that is closest to the soil surface.
