Identify the countries that made up the former Yugoslavia, including any territories that were part of the country at its dissolution.
Based on the provided context, the countries that made up the former Yugoslavia, including any territories that were part of the country at its dissolution, are:

1. Bosnia and Herzegovina
2. Croatia
3. Kosovo (as a Socialist Autonomous Province within Serbia)
4. Macedonia (now known as North Macedonia)
5. Montenegro
6. Serbia (including the Socialist Autonomous Provinces of Vojvodina and Kosovo)
7. Slovenia
8. Istria, Rijeka, and Zadar (territories acquired from Italy)

Note that the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia (FRY) and Serbia and Montenegro were formed after the breakup of Yugoslavia, but they are not considered to be part of the original country.
