3. Macedonia (also known as the Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia, FYR Macedonia)
4. Slovenia
5. Serbia and Montenegro (initially known as the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, later renamed to Serbia and Montenegro)
6. Montenegro (became an independent nation in 2006)
7. Kosovo (declared independence from Serbia in 2008 and became a FIBA member in 2015)

Note that the borders and territories of some of these countries have undergone changes since the dissolution of Yugoslavia, but the above list includes the countries that emerged as a result of the dissolution.
